---
import SectionHeading from './SectionHeading.astro';
---

<section class="wrap section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <SectionHeading id="about">About</SectionHeading>

  <div class="prose" data-reveal>
    <p>
      I studied Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning at Anurag University in Hyderabad, then came to Arizona State
      University for an M.S. in Data Science, Analytics and Engineering.
    </p>
    <p>
      The work I enjoy most is turning a model into something people can use in the middle of their day: an assistant inside
      the Zoom window they already have open, or a triage model that says why it ranked a ticket the way it did. I like the
      parts underneath too: pipelines, schemas, and concurrency.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before I build something, I decide how I will know it works. That is why CodeAtlas has hand-written ground truth, the
      ETL pipeline reconciles every record, and StreamBox has a load test. I write down the limits as well, like synthetic
      data or a single test machine.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .section {
    padding-top: var(--section-gap);
  }

  .prose {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
</style>
